Never underestimate the power of the humble potion of paralysis. 
Knight, the errr.... Knight (XL 16) was on his quest to kill the foul
dragon Ixoth knowing full well that the last knight foolish enough to
take on Ixoth without magic resistance met a gruesome end at the claws
of fell beast.  However, he felt duty bound to defeat Ixoth, no matter
the cost.  Standing at the steps leading into the lair of the beast,
Knight took quick inventory of his, well... inventory.  'ello,
whassis?  a potion of paralysis?  Hmmm... my noble upbringing tells me
that fighting foes whilst paralyzed is dishonorable, but King Arthur
is depending on me to bring back the mystical Magic Mirror of Merlin.

Oh well, it's my only hope.  Knight crept in to the lair of the beast
as quietly as his clanking armor would let him.  He dispatched the
noisome quasits and jellies with his trusty sword, Excalibur (clearly
Arthur had no need for it, what with sitting on his throne all day...)

Finding the entrance to the innermost pit of Ixoth's lair, the dreaded
beast appeared as if from out of thin air.  Sneering, Ixoth
disintegrated Knight's cloak of invisibility with but a blink of his
eye.  Undaunted, Knight merely laughed, for he had already zapped
himself with a wand designed for the very purpose of making oneself
invisible.

Lacking a means of free action, Knight knew he needed to get a step
away from Ixoth before he could safely use his evil potion.  He took a
step back, but Ixoth was upon him, batting him around with his claws
and foul breath.  Undaunted, our hero took yet another step back. 
Ixoth, with a gleam in his stony, red eyes, unleashed a fiery breath
from the depths of his throat.  Much to the dragon's chagrin, the
blast rebounded from a mirrored amulet nestled around Knight's neck.

With but a scant moment to act, Knight hurled his potion directly at
Ixoth's head, watching with delight as his aim was true.  Ixoth was
frozen with a strange look of horror on his scaly face.  Emboldened by
the sudden turn of events, and muttering a quick prayer to Lugh asking
forgiveness for such a cowardly fight, Knight stepped up to the fell
beast, positioned Excalibur directly at the dragons heart and plunged
it into a small crack between Ixoth's scales.  Finding his aim true,
the beast fell over, burbled up his last bloody breath, and expired.

The moral of this story, folks, is look VERY carefully at every item
in your possession before heading into a fight.  You may not be as
outmatched as you think.  That, and potions of paralysis kick some
serious ass when used correctly!

